# Gate State Lifecycle

All plugin-owned Hook gate state MUST use the canonical, host-neutral path:

```text
.github/github-plugin/state/
```

Cursor and Codex projections MUST copy the same `gate-state.mjs` helper and
MUST NOT create separate host-specific authorities. The generator may update
only its managed ignore and guidance block. It MUST NOT create gate files,
placeholder state, or recursively delete unknown files.

## Authority contract

Every authorizing gate MUST carry a version-1 `GateLifecycle` object with:

- `state: authority` and `authorizes: true`;
- the exact protected operation, including separate operations for each Ready
  reviewer request and each rebase phase;
- a cryptographically random, never-reused nonce;
- `issued_at` and `expires_at` exactly five minutes apart;
- `issued_at` no more than 60 seconds in the future;
- `consumed_at: null` and `receipt_expires_at: null`.

The lifecycle clock is authoritative. `written_at` remains fachliche evidence
only. Missing, malformed, mismatched, expired, future-skewed, old-version,
non-authorizing, or replayed state MUST fail closed before the protected
command.

## Atomic writer and claim

Owner Skills MUST call the shared lifecycle writer. It MUST write a temporary
file in the same directory, flush and sync it, publish it with a
non-overwriting atomic operation, reread and validate the final bytes, and
leave an existing destination untouched. Any write, sync, rename, lock, or
cleanup failure blocks before the external command.

Every protected Hook invocation MUST first atomically claim the authority out
of the canonical path before fachliche validation. A persistent plugin-owned
consumption marker keyed by nonce MUST survive process restarts. A command
failure, timeout, process crash, or failed later semantic check therefore
cannot make a valid gate reusable.

## Quarantine and legacy migration

Malformed, mismatched, expired, replayed, and non-authorizing states MUST be
quarantined into plugin-owned paths without recursive deletion. Only known
legacy gate filenames under `.cursor/hooks/state/` and `.codex/hooks/state/`
may be detected during the one release-generation migration. They are moved
to quarantine or reported as a bounded cleanup limitation and are never read
as authority. Unknown files and user-owned guidance remain untouched. After
the migration generation, legacy paths are not an authority source.

Abandoned temporary and processing files may be removed only when they match
the helper's plugin-owned bounded names and age rules. Cleanup diagnostics MUST
be sanitized, non-recursive, and separate from the protected command result.

## Receipts and rollback

Consuming one `pre-merge` authority may create exactly one
`post-merge-receipt.json`. A receipt MUST have `state: receipt`,
`authorizes: false`, operation `pre-merge`, the consumed nonce,
`consumed_at`, and a five-minute `receipt_expires_at`. The post-merge Hook
observes and atomically consumes/removes the receipt once. A second invocation
has no authority and cannot replay the merge.

New receipts and consumed-gate markers are intentionally incompatible with an
older plugin generation. Rollback MUST leave them unusable; an older version
may diagnose or quarantine them but MUST NOT restore them as authorizing state.
